{
 "id": "zenodo:22682542",
 "title": "The Dravidian Database: Reconstructed Lexicon of the Dravidian Subgroups Linked to the Dravidian Etymological Dictionary",
 "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/22682542",
 "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22682542",
 "description": "<p>This dataset unifies the reconstructed lexicon of the Dravidian language family into a single, structured resource. It links 15,629 reconstructed proto-forms &mdash; Starostin's six StarLing reconstruction databases imported in full at database granularity (12,868 records), Krishnamurti (2003) (891), and 1,870 reconstructions by the author &mdash; to 72,091 attested lemma records from 26 Dravidian languages digitized from the revised Dravidian Etymological Dictionary (DEDR; Burrow &amp; Emeneau 1984, DSAL digital edition).</p>\n<p>Every reconstruction carries two levels: source_classification, the level its source claims for it (for Starostin, the level of the StarLing database it comes from, with his own label in the note field), and evidence_classification, computed mechanically from the DEDR attestation as the deepest level supported by the attesting daughter languages. Comparing the two shows whether a source's claimed level is matched, exceeded, or unsupported by the evidence: of the 15,463 records with attestation data, 93.3% are supported at the level their source claims. Reconstructions from different sources for the same etymon are retained side by side rather than merged and every form is paired with a phonologically simplified companion form for fuzzy searching.</p>\n<p>New in version 1.2:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Starostin's databases were re-imported from a fresh crawl of StarLing, one record per database entry. The version 1.0 batch, whose records had been collapsed to one per root and labelled by attestation, was removed. No record credited to Starostin now carries a South Dravidian II, South Total Dravidian or Northern Dravidian label, which are not nodes of his classification;</li>\n<li>South Dravidian II in the evidence-based classification requires attestation in both Telugu and Gondi-Kui. Telugu-only support is assessed at Proto-Telugu, Gondi-Kui-only support at Gondi-Kui;</li>\n<li>the CLDF Wordlist (86,989 forms in 5,627 cognate sets, Glottolog identifiers)",
 "found_by_keywords": [
  "Indus script"
 ],
